<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1087 0 R
/E (There is a fatal loss of information in this process. Just as important as the value of a pixel in an image is the spatial information of which pixels are next to each other. A human eye, a cat's ear, or a car wheel only have meaning when several pixels are grouped together in a specific shape. But the moment you flatten the data into one dimension, the information about which pixels were originally above, below, or next to each other disappears. The neural network simply receives a list of 16 independent numbers.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
