/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1110 0 R
/E (Locality: Instead of looking at the entire image at once like FCN, it looks at a 'local' part of the image through a small window called a kernel. This is based on the fact that features in an image \(e.g. the human eye\) are not made up of individual pixels, but rather of a combination of surrounding pixels.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1111 0 R
/E (Parameter Sharing: A kernel that finds vertical lines in the upper left of an image can also find vertical lines in the lower right. Thus, a single kernel \(a single set of parameters\) is reused over the entire image. This 'parameter sharing' dramatically reduces the number of parameters to learn compared to FCN.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
