438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1113 0 R
/E (Padding: When performing convolution operations, there is a problem that the size of the feature map becomes smaller than the input image. In particular, pixels at the corners or borders of the image participate in the operation less often than the center, which may result in information loss. To prevent this, the edges of the input image are surrounded by a specific value \(usually 0\) and this is called padding. Adding padding can keep the size of the feature map the same as the input \(this is called 'Same' padding\).)
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
