/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1114 0 R
/E (Channel: Black and white images have one channel, but color images have three channels: R, G, and B. If the input image has multiple channels, the kernel must also have the corresponding number of channels \(depth\). For example, a kernel that processes a three-channel color image would be a 3D cube with three channels. The operation performs convolution on each channel and then adds the results to create a single number. In addition, multiple kernels can be used to detect different features \(vertical lines, horizontal lines, red, etc.\) at the same time. The number of kernels used is the number of channels in the output feature map.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
